Hooks — what they are

Hooks are just functions that let you use React features (state, side effects, context, etc.) inside function components. Before hooks existed, only class components could do things like hold state — function components were "dumb," just plain render functions. Hooks removed that limitation.

Rule: every hook name starts with use

useState, useEffect, useContext, useRef, useMemo, useCallback — all hooks. If you see use..., it's a hook.


